    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1209-a & 1266, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5452\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to service by\nmail provisions of, and jurisdiction over violations occurring on MTA\nomnibuses by the transit adjudication bureau of the New York city\ntransit authority\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill will allow any violations occurring on the MTA bus system to\nbe sent to the Transit Adjudication Bureau.\n\nSPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the Public Authorities law by giving provisions of\njurisdiction relating to violations on omnibuses to the Bureau of the\nNew York City Transit Authority.\n\nSections 2 and 3 state violations and penalties Section 4 gives\nprovisions for appeal of violations\n\nSection 5 amends the Public Authorities law by adding the punishment\nof a civil penalty by the bureau.\n\nSection 6 gives effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will allow any violations occurring on the MTA bus system to\nbe sent to the Transit Adjudication Bureau.  Currently, all\nenforcement actions taken on the MTA bus system must be sent to the\nNew York City court system. This will allow lower level violations to\nbe sent to the Transit Adjudication Bureau, where other violations\nthat occur on the MTA Transit and New York City Bus are current\nadjudicated.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
