    "lawCode": "Amd §§1209-a & 1266, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5452A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public authorities law, in\nrelation to service by mail provisions of, and jurisdiction over\nviolations occurring on metropolitan transportation authority\nomnibuses by the transit adjudication bureau of the New York city\ntransit authority\n\nPURPOSE: This bill gives authority to the Bureau of the New York City\nTransit Authority relating to violations occurring on MTA omnibuses.\n\nSPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the Public Authorities law by giving provisions of\njurisdiction relating to violations on omnibuses to the Bureau of the\nNew York City Transit Authority,\n\nSections 2 and 3 state violations and penalties Section 4 gives\nprovisions for appeal of violations\n\nSection 5 amends the Public Authorities law by adding the punishment\nof a civil penalty by the bureau.\n\nSection 6 gives effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: This bill will gives specific provisions for violations\non omnibuses that were not available before.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
